---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Danny Hoang | Networking | Infrastructure | Automation">
  <nav class="navbar">
    <div class="nav-container">
      <a href="/" class="nav-logo">DH<span>.</span></a>
      <div class="nav-links">
        <a href="#projects">Projects</a>
        <a href="#philosophy">Mindset</a>
        <a href="#skills">Skills</a>
        <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/vietthuhoang/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="nav-btn">LinkedIn</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <main>
    <header class="hero">
      <div class="hero-container">
        <div class="avatar-wrapper">
          <img src="/images/profile-photo.jpg" alt="Danny Hoang" class="hero-avatar" />
        </div>
        <div class="hero-content">
          <h1>Hi, I'm <span class="highlight">Danny Hoang</span></h1>
          <p class="tagline">Networking | Infrastructure | Automation</p>
          <div class="badge-row">
            <span class="badge">CCNA Certified</span>
            <span class="badge">Security+</span>
            <span class="badge">A+</span>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-bio">
            I build and experiment with network infrastructure, from Cisco lab topologies to
            containerized services running on Linux servers. My goal is to understand how systems actually
            work, from the physical network up through the applications that run on it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section id="projects" class="projects-section">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>Technical Projects</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="project-grid">
        <div class="project-card featured">
          <div class="card-content">
            <div class="card-header">
              <span class="category">Primary Lab / Infrastructure</span>
              <h3>Hybrid Homelab Infrastructure</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="img-container">
              <img src="/images/homelab-diagram.png" alt="Network diagram of hybrid homelab infrastructure showing Proxmox, Docker, and Tailscale topology" class="project-img" />
            </div>
            <div class="tags">
              <span>Proxmox</span> <span>Ansible</span> <span>Docker</span> <span>Tailscale</span>
            </div>
            <p class="project-description">
              Migrated my homelab from manual configuration ("ClickOps") to Infrastructure as Code.
              Designed a split topology that isolates core network services from compute workloads.
            </p>
            <a href="https://github.com/dannyhng/hybrid-homelab-infrastructure" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="project-link">View Documentation →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="project-card">
          <div class="card-content">
            <div class="card-header">
              <span class="category">ISP / Service Provider</span>
              <h3>MPLS L3VPN Backbone</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="img-container">
              <img src="/images/mpls-lab.png" alt="MPLS L3VPN lab topology diagram showing ISP backbone with VRF tenant isolation" class="project-img" />
            </div>
            <div class="tags">
              <span>MPLS</span> <span>MP-BGP</span> <span>VRFs</span> <span>EVE-NG</span>
            </div>
            <p>Built an MPLS backbone in my lab to simulate an ISP environment with VRF-based tenant isolation.</p>
            <a href="https://github.com/dannyhng/isp-mpls-l3vpn-lab" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="project-link">View Documentation →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="project-card">
          <div class="card-content">
            <div class="card-header">
              <span class="category">Enterprise Networking</span>
              <h3>Enterprise Network Topology Lab</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="img-container">
              <img src="/images/ccna-lab.png" alt="CCNA enterprise lab topology covering OSPF, HSRP, VLANs and wireless LAN controller" class="project-img" />
            </div>
            <div class="tags">
              <span>OSPF</span> <span>HSRP</span> <span>WLC</span> <span>ACLs</span>
            </div>
            <p>Built an enterprise-style lab covering major CCNA topics like VLAN segmentation,
              dynamic routing (OSPF), and high-availability (HSRP).</p>
            <a href="https://github.com/dannyhng/ccna-full-config-lab" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="project-link">View Documentation →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="philosophy" class="philosophy-section">
  <h2>The Logic Behind the Build</h2>

  <div class="philosophy-content">
    <div class="philosophy-image-wrapper">
      <img src="/images/car.jpeg" alt="Hands-on troubleshooting mindset" class="philosophy-img" />
    </div>

    <div class="philosophy-text">
      <p>
        Long before I was configuring switches, I was in the garage trying to figure out why something wasn't working. 
        Working on cars taught me something that no certification ever could. In any complex system, the problem 
        is rarely where you expect it to be. It's the small things. A loose ground. A vacuum leak. 
        A connection that looks fine until you actually pull on it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Finding those issues requires patience and a methodical approach, especially when everything on the surface 
        looks normal. That's the part most people skip. They see green lights and assume nothing is wrong. 
        But some of the most important problems are the quiet ones. The ones that don't throw errors, 
        don't cause outages, don't announce themselves at all. 
      </p>
      <p>
        The only way to find them is to actually look. Pull the data. Run the scan. Watch what the system is telling you beneath the surface.
        That's exactly what drew me to networking. The same instinct that makes me reach for a diagnostic scanner 
        on a car is the same instinct that makes me run a packet capture on a network that seems stable.
      </p>
      <p>
        What I've come to believe is that cars and networks have far more in common than most people would think. 
        They're both layered systems that demand respect for the fundamentals. They both reward the person who understands 
        not just what each component does, but how everything interacts. 
      </p>
      <p>
        That philosophy, staying curious, reading the data, never trusting "good enough," is what I bring to my work as a network professional. 
        Not just to keep things running, but to understand why they run, and to catch what others miss before it ever becomes a problem.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

    <section id="skills" class="skills-section">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>Core Stack</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="skills-container">
        <div class="skill-box">
          <h4>Networking</h4>
          <p>OSPF, BGP, MPLS, VLANs, VPN (Tailscale), Cisco IOS, pfSense</p>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-box">
          <h4>Automation</h4>
          <p>Python (Netmiko), Ansible, Terraform, PowerShell, Bash, Git</p>
        </div>
        <div class="skill-box">
          <h4>Infrastructure</h4>
          <p>Proxmox VE, Docker, Microsoft Entra ID, Windows Server 2022</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="contact" class="contact-section">
      <div class="contact-container">
        <h2>Get in Touch</h2>
        <p class="contact-sub">Open to network engineering, infrastructure, and DevOps opportunities.</p>
        <div class="contact-links">
          <a href="mailto:thuvhoang19@gmail.com" class="contact-card">
            <span class="contact-icon">✉</span>
            <span>thuvhoang19@gmail.com</span>
          </a>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/vietthuhoang/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="contact-card">
            <span class="contact-icon">in</span>
            <span>linkedin.com/in/vietthuhoang</span>
          </a>
          <a href="https://github.com/dannyhng" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="contact-card">
            <span class="contact-icon">GH</span>
            <span>github.com/dannyhng</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  <footer class="footer">
    <div class="footer-content">
      <p>© 2026 Danny Hoang | Portland, OR</p>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Layout>

<style>
  :root {
    --primary: #2563eb;
    --primary-dark: #1d4ed8;
    --bg: #ffffff;
    --text-main: #111827;
    --text-muted: #4b5563;
    --border: #e5e7eb;
    --card-bg: #f9fafb;
  }

  body { background-color: var(--bg); margin: 0; font-family: 'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif; scroll-behavior: smooth; }

  /* Navbar */
  .navbar { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 1rem 0; position: sticky; top: 0; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.9); backdrop-filter: blur(10px); z-index: 100; }
  .nav-container { max-width: 1000px; margin: auto; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; padding: 0 1.5rem; }
  .nav-logo { font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.5rem; color: var(--text-main); text-decoration: none; }
  .nav-logo span { color: var(--primary); }
  .nav-links { display: flex; gap: 2rem; align-items: center; }
  .nav-links a { text-decoration: none; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 500; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .nav-links a:hover { color: var(--primary); }
  .nav-btn { background: var(--text-main); color: white !important; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; }

  main { max-width: 1000px; margin: auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; }

  /* Hero */
  .hero { padding: 8rem 0; }
  .hero-container { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 4rem; }
  .avatar-wrapper { flex-shrink: 0; }
  .hero-avatar { width: 210px; height: 210px; border-radius: 50%; border: 5px solid var(--primary); object-fit: cover; box-shadow: 0 15px 35px rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.15); }
  h1 { font-size: 4rem; font-weight: 900; margin: 0; letter-spacing: -0.05em; line-height: 1; }
  .highlight { color: var(--primary); }
  .tagline { font-size: 1.5rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 0.5rem; font-weight: 500; }
  .badge-row { display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
  .badge { background: #eff6ff; color: var(--primary); padding: 0.35rem 1rem; border-radius: 99px; font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 700; border: 1px solid #dbeafe; }
  .hero-bio { font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 0; color: var(--text-muted); }

  /* Projects */
  .section-header { margin: 4rem 0 2rem 0; }
  .section-header h2 { font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .project-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 3rem; }
  .project-card.featured { grid-column: span 2; border-left: 8px solid var(--primary); }
  .project-card { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; background: white; transition: 0.4s; }
  .project-card:hover { transform: translateY(-8px); box-shadow: 0 25px 50px -12px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); border-color: var(--primary); }
  .card-content { padding: 3rem; }
  .category { font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--primary); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; }
  .img-container { background: #fdfdfd; border-radius: 14px; margin: 2rem 0; border: 1px solid var(--border); overflow: hidden; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; }
  .project-img { width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 500px; object-fit: contain; }
  .tags { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.6rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .tags span { font-size: 0.8rem; background: var(--card-bg); padding: 0.3rem 0.9rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); font-weight: 700; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .project-link { display: inline-block; font-weight: 800; color: var(--primary); text-decoration: none; margin-top: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 2px solid transparent; transition: 0.2s; }
  .project-link:hover { border-bottom-color: var(--primary); }

  /* Philosophy */
  .philosophy-section { margin: 10rem 0; padding: 5rem; background: var(--text-main); color: white; border-radius: 32px; overflow: hidden; }
  .philosophy-section h2 { color: var(--primary); font-size: 2.75rem; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; font-weight: 900; width: 100%; white-space: nowrap; }
  .philosophy-content { line-height: 1.7; }
  .philosophy-image-wrapper { float: right; width: 300px; margin-left: 3rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .philosophy-img { width: 100%; border-radius: 20px; border: 3px solid var(--primary); box-shadow: 20px 20px 0px rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.2); }
  .philosophy-text p { font-size: 1.1rem; opacity: 0.85; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
/* On mobile, we set white-space back to normal so the title doesn't cut off on small screens */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .philosophy-image-wrapper { float: none; width: 100%; margin-left: 0; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .philosophy-section h2 { font-size: 2rem; white-space: normal; }
}

  /* Skills */
  .skills-section { margin-top: 4rem; }
  .skills-container { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 2rem; margin-bottom: 4rem; }
  .skill-box { padding: 2.5rem; background: var(--card-bg); border-radius: 20px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .skill-box h4 { margin: 0 0 1.25rem 0; color: var(--primary); font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 800; border-bottom: 3px solid var(--primary); display: inline-block; padding-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  .skill-box p { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6; }

  /* Contact */
  .contact-section { margin: 4rem 0 8rem 0; }
  .contact-container { text-align: center; }
  .contact-container h2 { font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .contact-sub { font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .contact-links { display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 1.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .contact-card { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; padding: 1rem 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; text-decoration: none; color: var(--text-main); font-weight: 500; font-size: 0.95rem; transition: 0.2s; background: white; }
  .contact-card:hover { border-color: var(--primary); color: var(--primary); transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .contact-icon { width: 32px; height: 32px; background: #eff6ff; color: var(--primary); border-radius: 8px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 800; }

  /* Footer */
  .footer { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 3rem 0; background: var(--card-bg); }
  .footer-content { max-width: 1000px; margin: auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 500; }

  /* Responsive */
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .hero-container, .philosophy-container { flex-direction: column; text-align: center; gap: 3rem; }
    .project-grid, .skills-container { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .project-card.featured { grid-column: span 1; border-left: 8px solid var(--primary); }
    .philosophy-section { padding: 2rem; }
    .philosophy-image-wrapper { flex: 0 0 auto; width: 100%; }
    .philosophy-img { box-shadow: 10px 10px 0px rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.2); }
    h1 { font-size: 3rem; }
    .badge-row { justify-content: center; }
    .contact-links { flex-direction: column; align-items: center; }
  }
</style>